{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D13","page":1,"quote":"-0.006"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D14","page":1,"quote":"-0.017"},{"kind":"note","ref":"N2","page":1,"quote":"# FINISH  :  IZBP"}],"comment":"Dimensions D13 and D14 specify a tolerance band of 0.011 mm on the pin diameter, but note N2 calls for an IZBP (zinc) plating finish with no allowance made for the added coating thickness. The plating will push the finished size out of tolerance and prevent proper mating; the designer must reduce the basic size or widen the tolerance to account for the plating build-up."
    ,
"recommended_correction":"Reduce the nominal diameter or adjust the tolerance limits so that after IZBP plating the final size remains within the required fit."}]}
